  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Institute for Peace (EIP)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">European Institute for Peace 2025 (EIP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Active in over twenty locations around the world, the Institute combines the agility of an independent organisation with the diplomatic reach of its board and proximity to the European Union and to European states. 

The vision is a world where armed conflict and threats to life and livelihoods are reduced and resolved through effective dialogue, mediation, and inclusive peace processes. EIPs mission is to catalyse and invest in opportunities for non-violent conflict resolution in ways that respond to the needs and hopes of people most at risk and in doing so, to optimise Europe&#x2019;s contribution to sustainable peace.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">EIP &#xe4;r verksam i ett 20-tals platser runt om i v&#xe4;rlden. EIPs vision &#xe4;r en v&#xe4;rld d&#xe4;r v&#xe4;pnade konflikter och hot mot liv och f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjning reduceras och l&#xf6;ses genom effektiv dialog, medling och inkluderande fredsprocesser. EIPs uppdrag &#xe4;r att katalysera och investera i m&#xf6;jligheter till konfliktl&#xf6;sning p&#xe5; ett s&#xe4;tt som svarar mot behoven och f&#xf6;rhoppningarna hos de personer som &#xe4;r mest utsatta f&#xf6;r risker och att p&#xe5; s&#xe5; s&#xe4;tt optimera Europas bidrag till h&#xe5;llbar fred.</narrative>
  </description>
